# UI & Components

- **Components**: Always use Arrow Functions.
- **Exports**: Use `default export` ONLY for Next.js App Router special files (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx`, `global-error.tsx`, `template.tsx`, `default.tsx`). Use `named export` for all regular components.
- **App Router**: Separate Server/Client Components. Use `"use client"` strictly only when necessary.
- **A11y**: Use semantic HTML. Use `<button>`/`<a>` for clickables, not `<div>`.
- **Tailwind CSS v4**:
  - Sort classes using `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss`.
  - Use `rem` by default. Use `px` ONLY for `max-width` and `border` thickness.
- **Class Composition**:
  - Always use the `cn()` utility from `@/lib/utils` when composing conditional classNames. Do not use template literals or plain `clsx()` alone.
  - For components with style variants (color, size, etc.), define variants using `class-variance-authority` (cva), and merge them like `cn(buttonVariants({ variant, size }), className)`.
  - New components should always accept an external `className` prop and merge it as the last argument so callers can override styles.
- **Design Tokens (globals.css)**:
  - ALWAYS prioritize `globals.css` tokens. NEVER use arbitrary values (e.g., `bg-[#ff0000]`).
  - Colors: Use `--color-{name}-{shade}` format.
  - Typography: Use predefined classes like `text-{size}-{weight}`. Do not string multiple text utilities together.
- **Fonts**: **Pretendard** is the ONLY font. No custom letter-spacing.
- **Assets**: Use SVGR for vector icons. Static SVG for logos/banners.
